    "account": "QAOWNER",
    "width": 390,
    "text": "Schedule\nSched­uling rules\n\nSet staffing, weekly hours and recurring coverage so your team knows what a complete schedule needs.\n\nOn this page\nLocation staffing\nWeekly hours\nRecurring coverage\nTrades and coverage\n\nStaffing and hours save together. Coverage periods and policies save separately.\n\nLocation staffing\n\nChoose the minimum staff needed during overlapping shift times, and whether a designated lead must be present.\n\nMain Office\nStaffing per shift\nMinimum staff\npeople\nDesignated lead required\nWest Office\nStaffing per shift\nMinimum staff\npeople\nDesignated lead required\nWeekly hours\n13 people\n\nTargets guide balanced schedules. Maximums flag extra scheduled hours. Leave a target blank to leave it out of the hours review.\n\nFind a person\nNo target\n13\n\nFictional Owner\nQAOWNER · Owner · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nowner Fictional QA\npayroll-qa-owner · Owner · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nMorgan Rivera\nAUDIT-M · Manager · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nmanager Fictional QA\npayroll-qa-manager · Manager · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nreviewer Fictional QA\npayroll-qa-reviewer · Manager · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nRobin Fictional QA\npayroll-qa-b · Lead · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nTaylor Rivera\nAUDIT-LEAD · Lead · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nAlexandra Rivera\nAUDIT-E · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nCasey Rivera\nAUDIT-BREAK · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nJordan Rivera\nAUDIT-ON · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nMaría José Fictional QA\npayroll-qa-a · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nMaría José Rivera Santiago With A Long Name\nAUDIT-LONG · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\nRiley Rivera\nAUDIT-SWAP · Employee · Main Office\nTarget\nhrs\nMaximum\nhrs\n\nCouldn’t save your changes. They’re still here; try again.\n\nSave staffing and hours\nRecurring coverage\n14 periods\n\nAdd the periods you expect every week. The schedule can then flag open coverage, even before any shift is added.\n\nAdd coverage period\nMain Office\n7 periods · 7 days a week\nWest Office\n7 periods · 7 days a week\nTrades and coverage\n\nHow shift trades and coverage requests are approved, and how far ahead they must be sent and completed.\n\nHow trades and coverage work",
